== Campaign ==
Non-governmental organisations assessed that [[Political polarisation|polarisation]] was present during the electoral campaign period.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Tatalović |first=Žaklina |date=22 March 2022 |title=ENEMO: Funkcionerska kampanja i pritisci na birače su razlog za zabrinutost |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/enemo-funkcionerska-kampanja-i-pritisci-na-birace-su-razlog-za-zabrinutost/ |access-date=1 April 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=21 February 2022 |title=Masovne zloupotrebe i izrazita neravnopravnost u "kampanji pre kampanje" |url=https://crta.rs/masovne-zloupotrebe-i-izrazita-neravnopravnost-u-kampanji-pre-kampanje/ |access-date=31 March 2022 |website=CRTA |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=3 March 2022 |title=Mediji da ne doprinose polarizaciji društva |url=https://novaekonomija.rs/vesti-iz-zemlje/mediji-da-ne-doprinose-polarizaciji-dru%C5%A1tva |access-date=31 March 2022 |website=Nova Ekonomija |language=sr |archive-date=17 March 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220317055950/https://novaekonomija.rs/vesti-iz-zemlje/mediji-da-ne-doprinose-polarizaciji-dru%C5%A1tva |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=20 February 2022 |title=Klačar: Kampanja za izbore će biti takmičarska i kreativna |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/politika/klacar-kampanja-za-izbore-ce-biti-takmicarska-i-kreativna_1315838.html |access-date=31 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref> The Bureau of Social Research (BIRODI) claimed that the pro-government media dominated during the period, while Transparency Serbia claimed that the ruling party had a significant domination in the media.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bjelotomić |first=Snežana |date=22 March 2022 |title=BIRODI: Vučić dominates media in his election campaign |url=https://www.serbianmonitor.com/en/birodi-vucic-dominates-media-in-his-election-campaign/ |access-date=22 March 2022 |website=Serbian Monitor |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=31 March 2022 |title=Transparentnost: Izrazita medijska dominacija vladajuće stranke i kandidata |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/transparentnost-izrazita-medijska-dominacija-vladajuce-stranke-i-kandidata/ |access-date=31 March 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref> According to multiple researches that were conducted by BIRODI, the media became vehicles of [[Media propaganda|propaganda]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=5 March 2022 |title=BIRODI: Mediji se pred izbore pretvaraju u sredstva propagande |url=https://www.021.rs/story/Info/Srbija/299455/BIRODI-Mediji-se-pred-izbore-pretvaraju-u-sredstva-propagande.html |access-date=5 March 2022 |website=021.rs |language=sr}}</ref><ref name=":24">{{Cite web |date=22 March 2022 |title=BIRODI: Učesnici predizborne kampanje evrointegracijama posvetili manje od jedan odsto vremena |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/birodi-ucesnici-predizborne-kampanje-evrointegracijama-posvetili-manje-od-jedan-odsto-vremena/ |access-date=22 March 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref> CRTA stated that the electoral campaign period was allegedly in worse conditions than during the campaign period of the 2020 parliamentary election.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Komazec |first=Marija |date=31 March 2022 |title=Istraživanje Crte: Izborna kampanja u lošijim uslovima nego ona iz 2020. godine |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/istrazivanje-crte-izborna-kampanja-u-losijim-uslovima-nego-ona-iz-2020-godine/ |access-date=31 March 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref> The pre-election delegation of the [[Parliamentary Assembly of the Council of Europe]] (PACE) had stated that the atmosphere during the campaign remained calm and that all political contestants were able to campaign freely. It had also expressed concern over possible pressure on voters and fear of irregularities on election day.<ref>{{Cite web |date=4 March 2022 |title=Predizborna delegacija PSSE: Opšta atmosfera mirna, svi takmičari mogu slobodno da vode kampanju |url=https://www.euronews.rs/izbori-2022/vesti/39695/predizborna-delegacija-psse-opsta-atmosfera-mirna-svi-takmicari-mogu-slobodno-da-vode-kampanju/vest |access-date=5 March 2022 |website=Euronews |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=4 March 2022 |title=Delegacija SE o poseti Srbiji: Izborna kampanja slobodna, bez ograničenja |url=http://www.rts.rs/page/stories/sr/Izbori2022/story/3364/vesti/4726473/se-delgacija-srbija-izbori-.html |access-date=5 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Serbia |language=sr}}</ref> The Temporary Supervisory Body, which is operated by REM, claimed that BIRODI and CRTA published claims which were not substantiated.<ref>{{Cite web |date=22 February 2022 |title=Privremeno nadzorno telo: BIRODI se rukovodi duplim standardima u monitoringu medija |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/privremeno-nadzorno-telo-birodi-se-rukovodi-duplim-standardima-u-monitoringu-medija/ |access-date=22 March 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=31 March 2022 |title=Zekić: CRTA na konferenciji iznela "netačne i tendenciozne" podatke o kampanji |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/zekic-crta-na-konferenciji-iznela-netacne-i-tendenciozne-podatke-o-kampanji/ |access-date=31 March 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref>

To boost the electoral turnout, CRTA cooperated with the [[Nova S]] television channel by creating the {{Ill|italic=y|Zato, glasaj!|sr|Зато, гласај!}} show.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Jelovac |first=Jelena |date=8 March 2022 |title=Zato glasaj: Počinje nova emisija na televiziji Nova S |url=https://nova.rs/vesti/politika/zato-glasaj-sutra-pocinje-nova-emisija-na-televiziji-nova-s/ |access-date=22 March 2022 |website=NOVA portal |language=sr-RS}}</ref> The [[Radio Television of Serbia]], among other news channels, organised debates and program presentations during the campaign.<ref>{{Cite web |date=30 March 2022 |title=Biljana Stojković na RTS-u predstavila program za predsedničke izbore |url=http://www.rts.rs/page/stories/sr/Izbori2022/story/3392/predstavljanje/4759609/biljana-stojkovic-rts-program-predsednicki-izbori.html |access-date=31 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Serbia |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=30 March 2022 |title=Miloš Jovanović za RTS o programu za predsedničke izbore |url=http://www.rts.rs/page/stories/sr/Izbori2022/story/3392/predstavljanje/4759597/milos-jovanovic-rts-program-predsednicki-izbori.html |access-date=31 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Serbia |language=sr}}</ref> Multiple non-governmental organisations also announced their participation in monitoring the elections, such as ENEMO, CRTA, CeSID, [[Organization for Security and Co-operation in Europe|OSCE]], and delegates from PACE.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2 March 2022 |title=ENEMO: Akreditovano šest eksperata i 10 dugoročnih posmatrača za parlamentarne izbore |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/enemo-akreditovani-eksperti-i-dugorocni-posmatraci-za-parlamentarne-izbore/ |access-date=5 March 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Valtner |first=Lidija |date=21 February 2022 |title=Posmatrači izbora: U zaštiti izbornog prava bićemo orijentir i podrška građanima |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/posmatraci-izbora-u-zastiti-izbornog-prava-bicemo-orijentir-i-podrska-gradjanima/ |access-date=5 March 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=23 February 2022 |title=Otvorena posmatračka misija OEBS za izbore u Srbiji |url=https://www.b92.net/info/izbori2022/vesti.php?yyyy=2022&mm=02&dd=23&nav_id=2110273 |access-date=5 March 2022 |website=B92 |language=sr-Latn-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=29 March 2022 |title=I delegacija PS Saveta Evrope posmatraće izbore u Srbiji |url=https://www.b92.net/info/izbori2022/vesti.php?yyyy=2022&mm=03&dd=29&nav_id=2130505 |access-date=29 March 2022 |website=B92 |language=sr-Latn-RS}}</ref> Opposition parties also hired election controllers to lower the potential of [[electoral fraud]]; CRTA announced that it had hired 3,000 election observers for the election.<ref>{{Cite web |date=25 March 2022 |title=Izborni dan pratiće 3.000 posmatrača Crte |url=https://www.politika.rs/sr/clanak/503057/Izborni-dan-pratice-3-000-posmatraca-Crte |access-date=27 March 2022 |website=Politika |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Filipov |first=Ljubomir |date=4 March 2022 |title=Kontrolori najvažniji za regularnost izbora, iz opozicije najavljuju da će pokriti sva biračka mesta |url=https://www.juznevesti.com/Politika/Kontrolori-najvazniji-za-regularnost-izbora-iz-opozicije-najavljuju-da-ce-pokriti-sva-biracka-mesta.sr.html |access-date=5 March 2022 |website=Južne vesti |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=28 March 2022 |title=Jovanović: Imaćemo 20.000 kontrolora, pokrićemo više od 99 odsto biračkih mesta |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/jovanovic-imacemo-20-000-kontrolora-pokricemo-vise-od-99-odsto-birackih-mesta/ |access-date=31 March 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref> During the last campaign week, organisations noted the appearance of "phantom voters", signalling potential electoral fraud.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Čongradin |first=Snežana |date=29 March 2022 |title=Fantomski glasači tek vrh ledenog brega nepravilnosti |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/fantomski-glasaci-tek-vrh-ledenog-brega-nepravilnosti/ |access-date=29 March 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=28 March 2022 |title=Fantomski birači: Pa šta |url=https://www.vreme.com/vesti/fantomski-biraci-pa-sta/ |access-date=29 March 2022 |website=Vreme |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Nešić |first=Nenad |date=28 March 2022 |title=Ovo je vreme fantomskih birača? Ima ih u biračkom spisku, ali ne i na adresi... |language=sr-RS |work=N1 |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/ovo-je-vreme-fantomskih-biraca-ima-ih-u-birackom-spisku-ali-ne-i-na-adresi/ |access-date=29 March 2022}}</ref> The [[election silence]] began on 1 April, and it lasted until the closure of polling stations on 3 April.<ref>{{Cite web |date=31 March 2022 |title=Još danas kampanja, u ponoć izborna tišina |url=https://www.b92.net/info/izbori2022/vesti.php?yyyy=2022&mm=03&dd=31&nav_id=2131731 |access-date=31 March 2022 |website=B92 |language=sr-Latn-RS}}</ref> Transparency Serbia noted that the campaign period was the most expensive one since 2004.<ref>{{Cite web |date=6 April 2022 |title=Transparentnost: Najskuplja kampanja od 2004, građane košta 15,7 miliona evra |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/transparentnost-najskuplja-kampanja-od-2004-gradjane-kosta-157-miliona-evra/ |access-date=6 April 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref>

=== Participating parties and coalitions ===
[[File:Glasački listić za izbor narodnih poslanika Narodne skupštine 3. aprila 2022. godine.png|thumb|upright=0.7|The parliamentary election ballot which contains all 19 ballot lists.]]
SNS and its coalition partners secured a supermajority in the parliament after the 2020 parliamentary election, with no official opposition represented in the parliament itself.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Janjević|first=Darko|date=20 June 2020|title=Serbia elections: Who's left besides Vucic?|url=https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-elections-whos-left-besides-vucic/a-53869625|url-status=live|access-date=5 November 2021|website=Deutsche Welle|language=en-GB|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200621160746/https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-elections-whos-left-besides-vucic/a-53869625 |archive-date=21 June 2020 }}</ref> In early May 2021, Vučić sent a proposal to [[Aleksandar Šapić]], the leader of the [[Serbian Patriotic Alliance]] (SPAS), about the merger of two parties.<ref>{{cite web|last=Krstović|first=Anđela|date=5 May 2021|title=Vučić saopštio: Ujediniće se SNS i Šapićev SPAS|url=https://nova.rs/vesti/politika/vucic-saopstio-ujedinice-se-sns-i-sapicev-spas/|access-date=30 January 2022|website=NOVA portal|language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|date=5 May 2021|title=Vučić pozvao Šapića na ujedinjenje|url=https://www.rts.rs/page/stories/sr/story/9/politika/4362332/vucic-predsednistvo-stranke-sapic-ujedinjenje.html|url-status=live|access-date=5 May 2021|website=Radio Television of Serbia|language=sr|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210505174850/https://www.rts.rs/page/stories/sr/story/9/politika/4362332/vucic-predsednistvo-stranke-sapic-ujedinjenje.html |archive-date=5 May 2021 }}</ref> Šapić announced his willingness to merge his party into SNS, and the merge occurred on 26 May.<ref>{{cite web|date=26 May 2021|title=Šapić gasi SPAS zbog ujedinjenja sa SNS|url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/danas-sapic-gasi-spas-zbog-ujedinjenja-sa-sns/|access-date=30 January 2022|website=N1|language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|last=Popović|first=Aleksandra|date=26 May 2021|title=SPAS usvojio predlog Šapića o uključenju u SNS|url=https://www.danas.rs/politika/spas-usvojio-predlog-sapica-o-ukljucenju-u-sns/|access-date=30 January 2022|website=Danas|language=sr}}</ref> He was subsequently promoted to vice-president of SNS,<ref>{{cite web|date=29 May 2021|title=SPAS zvanično pristupio SNS, Šapić izabran za potpredsednika Glavnog odbora|url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/spas-pristupio-sns-vucic-porucio-dobrodosli-u-svojub-stranku/|access-date=30 January 2022|website=N1|language=sr}}</ref> while its MPs joined the SNS-led parliamentary group in early June.<ref>{{Cite web|date=7 June 2021|title=Poslanici SPAS zvanično pripojeni grupi Aleksandra Vučića|url=https://nova.rs/vesti/politika/poslanici-spas-zvanicno-pripojeni-grupi-aleksandra-vucica/|access-date=16 October 2021|website=NOVA portal|language=sr-RS}}</ref> SNS had also affirmed its position to continue their cooperation with SPS.<ref>{{Cite web|date=26 October 2021|title=Vučić: SNS i SPS nastavljaju saradnju i u budućnosti|url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/vucic-sns-i-sps-nastavljaju-saradnju-i-u-buducnosti/|access-date=27 October 2021|website=N1|language=sr-RS}}</ref> After a meeting in January 2022, it was announced to the public that they would participate with a joint presidential candidate while participating on separate ballot lists for the parliamentary election.<ref>{{Cite web|date=29 January 2022|title=SNS i SPS s posebnim listama na izbore, zajednički kandidat za predsednika|url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/sastanak-sps-i-sns/|access-date=29 January 2022|website=N1|language=sr-RS}}</ref> In February, Dačić was chosen as the SPS ballot representative,<ref>{{Cite web|last=Gajić|first=Petar|date=12 February 2022|title=Dačić nosilac svih lista SPS i kandidat za premijera, za predsednika - Vučić|url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/dacic-nosilac-svih-lista-sps-i-kandidat-za-premijera-za-predsednika-vucic/|access-date=12 February 2022|website=N1|language=sr-RS|archive-date=12 February 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220212135212/https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/dacic-nosilac-svih-lista-sps-i-kandidat-za-premijera-za-predsednika-vucic/|url-status=dead}}</ref> while Vučić was chosen as SNS ballot representative.<ref>{{Cite web|date=13 February 2022|title=Vučić nosilac svih lista SNS, Grujičić prva na republičkoj, Šapić na beogradskoj|url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/vucic-nosilac-svih-lista-sns-grujicic-prva-na-republickoj-sapic-na-beogradskoj/|access-date=13 February 2022|website=N1|language=sr-RS}}</ref>

Parties that were a part of the UOPS coalition resumed their cooperation in mid-2021,<ref>{{cite web|date=12 June 2021|title=Grbović: PSG najbliži zajedničkoj listi sa DS i SSP|url=https://www.danas.rs/politika/grbovic-psg-najblizi-zajednickoj-listi-sa-ds-i-ssp/|access-date=30 January 2022|website=Danas|language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|date=15 October 2021|title=Đilas: Neophodno je jedinstvo svih opozicionih snaga ako želimo promene u Srbiji|url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/djilas-neophodno-je-jedinstvo-svih-opozicionih-snaga-ako-zelimo-promene-u-srbiji/|access-date=23 October 2021|website=N1|language=sr-RS}}</ref> and in October 2021, SSP announced that it would be forming a joint opposition coalition.<ref>{{Cite web|date=22 October 2021|title=Đilas: SSP, DS, PSG, PZP i NS će zajedno doneti odluku o učešću na izborima|url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/djilas-ssp-ds-psg-pzp-i-ns-ce-zajedno-doneti-odluku-o-ucescu-na-izborima/|access-date=23 October 2021|website=N1|language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|date=14 October 2021|title=Mediji: SSP, DS i Narodna stranka postigli dogovor o zajedničkoj listi|url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/mediji-ssp-ds-i-narodna-stranka-postigli-dogovor-o-zajednickoj-listi/|access-date=16 October 2021|website=N1|language=sr-RS}}</ref> Talks about the formation were held until 23 November,<ref>{{Cite web|last=Valtner|first=Lidija|date=15 October 2021|title=Važan dogovor SSP, DS i NS o prvih 80 na listi|url=https://www.danas.rs/politika/vazan-dogovor-ssp-ds-i-ns-o-prvih-80-na-listi/|url-status=live|access-date=16 October 2021|website=Danas|language=sr-RS|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211015065121/https://www.danas.rs/politika/vazan-dogovor-ssp-ds-i-ns-o-prvih-80-na-listi/ |archive-date=15 October 2021 }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|date=15 November 2021|title=Borko Stefanović očekuje dogovor opozicije u narednih desetak dana|url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/borko-stefanovic-ocekuje-dogovor-opozicije-u-narednih-desetak-dana/|access-date=16 November 2021|website=N1|language=sr-RS}}</ref> after which it was announced to the public that SSP would lead the coalition alongside DS, Narodna, PSG, and other minor parties and movements.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Latković|first=Nataša|date=23 November 2021|title=SSP, DS, Narodna stranka i PSG postigli dogovor: Zajedno izlaze na izbore|url=https://nova.rs/vesti/politika/ssp-ds-i-psg-postigli-dogovor-zajedno-izlaze-na-izbore/|access-date=23 November 2021|website=NOVA portal|language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|date=21 November 2021|title=Opozicija ima načelni dogovor oko nastupa na izborima|url=https://direktno.rs/politika/383777/zoran-lutovac-nacelni-dogovor-opozicija-utisak-nedelje.html|url-status=live|access-date=22 November 2021|website=Direktno|language=sr|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211121221640/https://direktno.rs/politika/383777/zoran-lutovac-nacelni-dogovor-opozicija-utisak-nedelje.html |archive-date=21 November 2021 }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Latković|first=Nataša|date=24 November 2021|title=OTKRIVAMO Ovako će opozicija podeliti kvote na izbornoj listi|url=https://nova.rs/vesti/politika/otkrivamo-ovako-ce-opozicija-podeliti-kvote-na-izbornoj-listi/|access-date=24 November 2021|website=NOVA portal|language=sr-RS}}</ref> [[Marinika Tepić]] was chosen as their parliamentary representative.<ref>{{Cite web|date=24 November 2021|title=Nova: Marinika Tepić predvodi opozicionu listu, dogovoren i raspored kvota|url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/nova-marinika-tepic-predvodi-opozicionu-listu-dogovoren-i-raspored-kvota/|access-date=24 November 2021|website=N1|language=sr-RS}}</ref> It was officially formalised in February 2022, under the name of [[United for the Victory of Serbia]] (UZPS).<ref>{{Cite web|last=Popović|first=Aleksandra|date=2 February 2022|title=Tepić: Koalicija "Ujedinjena Srbija" pobediće na izborima 3. apila|url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/tepic/|access-date=2 February 2022|website=Danas|language=sr-RS}}</ref> Dveri, which was a part of the SZS coalition, declined to join their list,<ref>{{Cite web|date=27 October 2021|title=Nova.rs: Dveri samostalno izlaze na izbore, Obradović kandidat za predsednika|url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/nova-rs-dveri-samostalno-izlaze-na-izbore-obradovic-kandidat-za-predsednika/|access-date=5 November 2021|website=N1|language=sr-RS}}</ref> and instead it formed the "Patriotic Bloc" with minor right-wing parties in December 2021.<ref>{{Cite web|date=14 October 2021|title=Obradović: Predvodićemo patriotsku kolonu, ne vidimo sebe u obnovljenoj DS|url=https://www.danas.rs/politika/obradovic-predvodicemo-patriotsku-kolonu-ne-vidimo-sebe-u-obnovljenoj-ds/|url-status=live|access-date=16 October 2021|website=Danas|language=sr-RS|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211014093213/https://www.danas.rs/politika/obradovic-predvodicemo-patriotsku-kolonu-ne-vidimo-sebe-u-obnovljenoj-ds/ |archive-date=14 October 2021 }}</ref><ref name=":2">{{Cite web|last=Gajić|first=Petar|date=2 December 2021|title=Formiran patriotski blok, Boško Obradović kandidat za predsednika Srbije|url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/formiran-patriotski-blok-novi-ljudi-za-promenu-sistema/|access-date=4 December 2021|website=N1|language=sr-RS}}</ref> DJB had also announced their participation in the election,<ref>{{Cite web|date=2 November 2021|title=Dosta je bilo: Imaćemo svog kandidata na predsedničkim izborima|url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/dosta-je-bilo-imacemo-svog-kandidata-na-predsednickim-izborima/|url-status=live|access-date=5 November 2021|website=N1|language=sr-RS|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211103140520/https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/dosta-je-bilo-imacemo-svog-kandidata-na-predsednickim-izborima/ |archive-date=3 November 2021 }}</ref> and in late November, they began cooperating with [[Healthy Serbia]] (ZS) and the [[Anti-vaccine activism|anti-vax]] "[[I live for Serbia]]" movement to form a "[[Sovereignists (Serbia)|Sovereignist Bloc]]".<ref>{{Cite web|date=30 November 2021|title=Stamatović i Radulović prave suverenistički blok, Dveri sebe vide kao desnu kolonu|url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/stamatovic-i-radulovic-prave-suverenisticki-blok-dveri-sebe-vide-kao-desnu-kolonu/|url-status=live|access-date=4 December 2021|website=Danas|language=sr-RS|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211130192052/https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/stamatovic-i-radulovic-prave-suverenisticki-blok-dveri-sebe-vide-kao-desnu-kolonu/ |archive-date=30 November 2021 }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|date=24 January 2022|title=Dosta je bilo, Zdrava Srbija i Živim za Srbiju izlaze na izbore na listi Suverenisti|url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/dosta-je-bilo-zdrava-srbija-i-zivim-za-srbiju-izlaze-na-izbore-na-listi-suverenisti/|access-date=29 January 2022|website=Danas|language=sr-RS}}</ref>

In June 2021, [[Nebojša Zelenović]], the leader of ZZS formed a coalition named "Action" in which 28 minor environmentalist civic groups and political movements joined due to their support for the "Green Agreement for Serbia".<ref>{{cite web|date=5 June 2021|title=Osnovana otvorena građanska platforma "Akcija"|url=https://www.danas.rs/politika/osnovana-gradjanska-platforma-akcija/|access-date=30 January 2022|website=Danas|language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|date=6 June 2021|title=Zelenović osniva "zelene" u Srbiji|url=https://www.danas.rs/politika/zelenovic-osniva-zelene-u-srbiji/|access-date=30 January 2022|website=Danas|language=sr}}</ref> Activist [[Aleksandar Jovanović Ćuta]] announced in mid-November that the "Ecological Uprising" movement would participate in the elections,<ref>{{cite web|date=11 November 2021|title=Jovanović: Pokret Ekološki ustanak izlazi na izbore na svim nivoima|url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/jovanovic-pokret-ekoloski-ustanak-izlazi-na-izbore-na-svim-nivoima/|access-date=16 November 2021|website=N1|language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|date=11 November 2021|title=Pokret Ekološki ustanak izlazi na izbore na svim nivoima|url=https://beta.rs/vesti/politika-vesti-srbija/154921-pokret-ekolo-ki-ustanak-izlazi-na-izbore-na-svim-nivoima|url-status=live|access-date=16 November 2021|website=Novinska agencija Beta|language=sr|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211111190700/https://beta.rs/vesti/politika-vesti-srbija/154921-pokret-ekolo-ki-ustanak-izlazi-na-izbore-na-svim-nivoima |archive-date=11 November 2021 }}</ref> and on 14 November, he signed an agreement with Zelenović to participate on a joint list.<ref>{{cite web|date=14 November 2021|title=Ćuta otkrio s kim će na izbore: Za ovo treba biti lud, mogao sam da ostanem superheroj|url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/cuta-otkrio-s-kim-ce-na-izbore-za-ovo-treba-biti-lud-mogao-sam-ostati-heroj/|access-date=16 November 2021|website=N1|language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|date=14 November 2021|title=Zelenović i Ćuta potpisali sporazum, "zeleno-levi" blok izlazi na izbore|url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/zelenovic-i-cuta-potpisali-sporazum-zeleno-levi-blok-izlazi-na-izbore/|access-date=16 November 2021|website=N1|language=sr-RS}}</ref> The [[Do not let Belgrade drown]] (NDB) movement had also agreed to join their coalition, which was formalised in January 2022, under the name [[We Must (Serbia)|We Must]].<ref name=":22">{{cite web|date=19 January 2022|title=Formirana zeleno-leva koalicija "Moramo"|url=https://nova.rs/vesti/politika/formirana-zeleno-leva-koalicija-moramo/|access-date=19 January 2022|website=NOVA portal|language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref name=":32">{{Cite web|date=19 January 2022|title=Zajedno za Srbiju, Ne davimo Beograd i Ekološki ustanak u koaliciji "Moramo"|url=https://www.021.rs/story/Info/Srbija/295536/Zajedno-za-Srbiju-Ne-davimo-Beograd-i-Ekoloski-ustanak-u-koaliciji-Moramo.html|access-date=19 January 2022|website=www.021.rs|language=sr}}</ref>

A right-wing coalition was supposed to be formed in which POKS, [[National Network (Serbia)|National Network]] (NM) led by [[Vladan Glišić]], [[Serbian Party Oathkeepers]] (SSZ) and DSS would take part, although this idea was dismissed, and a coalition and party protocol were formed and signed shortly after.<ref>{{cite web|last=Milenković|first=Mirjana|date=2 December 2020|title=Gojković: Biračima je dosta neprincipijelnih koalicija|url=https://www.danas.rs/politika/gojkovic-biracima-je-dosta-neprincipijelnih-koalicija/|access-date=30 January 2022|website=Danas|language=sr}}</ref> In January 2021, DSS and POKS signed an agreement,<ref>{{cite web|date=26 January 2021|title=DSS i POKS potpisali Sporazum o zajedničkom delovanju|url=https://www.danas.rs/politika/dss-i-poks-potpisali-sporazum-o-zajednickom-delovanju/|access-date=30 January 2022|website=Danas|language=sr}}</ref> and in May, with 19 other movements and civic groups, they formed the [[National Democratic Alternative (Serbia)|National Democratic Alternative]] (NADA),<ref>{{cite web|date=6 May 2021|title=POKS, DSS i 19 udruženja i grupa građana potpisali koalicioni sporazum|url=https://www.danas.rs/politika/poks-dss-i-19-udruzenja-i-grupa-gradjana-potpisali-koalicioni-sporazum/|access-date=30 January 2022|website=Danas|language=sr}}</ref> while far-right parties NM and SSZ signed a protocol between two parties in February 2021.<ref>{{cite web|date=17 February 2021|title=Potpisan protokol o saradnji Srpske stranke Zavetnici i Narodne mreže|url=https://www.danas.rs/politika/potpisan-protokol-o-saradnji-srpske-stranke-zavetnici-i-narodne-mreze/|access-date=30 January 2022|website=Danas|language=sr}}</ref> At the time of the general election, the POKS leadership remained disputed, although the faction around [[Žika Gojković]] legally claimed the leadership of the party.<ref>{{Cite web |date=3 January 2022 |title=Deo rukovodstva POKS: Vojislav Mihailović izabran za predsednika stranke |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/deo-rukovodstva-poks-vojislav-mihailovic-izabran-za-predsednika-stranke/ |access-date=1 April 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=23 February 2022 |title=RIK proglasio izbornu listu Dveri i frakcije POKS-a koju predvodi Žika Gojković |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/rik-proglasio-izbornu-listu-dveri-i-frakcije-poks-a-koju-predvodi-zika-gojkovic/ |access-date=1 April 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref>

In May 2021, SDS signed a protocol with the centrist coalition "Toleration".<ref>{{cite web|date=23 May 2021|title=SDS i koalicija "Tolerancija" potpisale protokol o političkoj saradnji|url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/sds-i-koalicija-tolerancija-potpisale-protokol-o-politickoj-saradnji/|access-date=30 January 2022|website=N1|language=sr}}</ref> In November, it was announced that Democrats of Serbia, a splinter from DS which was formed in February 2021,<ref>{{Cite web|last=Stojanović|first=Ivana|date=28 February 2021|title=Održan skup "Demokrata Srbije", na čelu novog pokreta Branislav Lečić|url=https://insajder.net/sr/sajt/vazno/22948/Odr%C5%BEan-skup-%E2%80%9EDemokrata-Srbije%E2%80%9C-na-%C4%8Delu-novog-pokreta-Branislav-Le%C4%8Di%C4%87.htm|access-date=28 February 2021|website=Insajder|language=sr}} {{Dead link|date=September 2026 |bot=InternetArchiveBot }}</ref> would merge into SDS; the merge was formalised in February 2022.<ref>{{Cite web|date=13 November 2021|title=Demokrate Srbije se utapaju u SDS|url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/demokrate-srbije-se-utapaju-u-sds/|access-date=16 November 2021|website=N1|language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=5 February 2022 |title=Ujedinile se Socijaldemokratska stranka i Demokrate Srbije |url=http://www.rts.rs/page/stories/sr/story/9/politika/4689513/socijaldemokratska-stranka-demokrate-srbije-ujedinjenje.html |access-date=25 August 2022 |website=Radio Television of Serbia |language=sr}}</ref> In late May, Nova formed a coalition with a minor movement led by [[Marko Bastać]],<ref>{{cite web|date=8 June 2021|title=Ko se udružuje zarad izbornih koalicija?|url=https://www.danas.rs/politika/ko-se-udruzuje-zarad-izbornih-koalicija/|access-date=30 January 2022|website=Danas|language=sr}}</ref> but the coalition was later dissolved in September.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Valtner|first=Lidija|date=22 September 2021|title=Bastać napustio grupaciju oko SDS, iz SDS mu poručuju da se odluči|url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/bastac-napustio-grupaciju-oko-sds-iz-sds-mu-porucuju-da-se-odluci/|url-status=live|access-date=5 November 2021|website=Danas|language=sr-RS|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211029223325/https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/bastac-napustio-grupaciju-oko-sds-iz-sds-mu-porucuju-da-se-odluci/ |archive-date=29 October 2021 }}</ref> Later during 2021, SDS formed a coalition with Nova and the [[Civic Democratic Forum]] (GDF).<ref>{{Cite web|last=Milenković|first=M. R.|date=11 January 2022|title=Nova stranka, SDS i GDF pozvali građane da zaokruže NE na referendumu u nedelju|url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/nova-stranka-sds-i-gdf-pozvali-gradjane-da-zaokruze-ne-na-referendumu-u-nedelju/|access-date=29 January 2022|website=Danas|language=sr-RS}}</ref> Tadić presented his coalition in late February 2022, which included Nova and five minor movements.<ref>{{Cite web |date=24 February 2022 |title=Predstavljena koalicija "Boris Tadić - Ajmo ljudi": Borimo se za demokratiju |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/predstavljena-koalicija-boris-tadic-ajmo-ljudi-borimo-se-za-demokratiju/ |access-date=5 March 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref>

