=== Issues ===
The campaign period began shortly after the dissolution of the National Assembly.<ref name=":19" /> Parties that took part in the environmental protests stated their opposition to [[Rio Tinto (corporation)|Rio Tinto]] during the electoral campaign, while some parties, such as SRS, stated its support.<ref>{{Cite web|date=15 February 2022|title=Zelenović: Glas za "Moramo" je glas protiv Rio Tinta|url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/zelenovic-glas-za-moramo-je-glas-protiv-rio-tinta/|access-date=18 February 2022|website=N1|language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|date=25 January 2022|title=SRS za litijum: Ucenjivanje, Vlada nikako ne sme da prihvati trajnu zabranu|url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/srs-za-litijum-ucenjivanje-vlada-nikako-ne-sme-da-prihvati-trajnu-zabranu/|access-date=18 February 2022|website=N1|language=sr-RS}}</ref> Although according to CeSID, following the beginning of the [[2022 Russian invasion of Ukraine|Russian invasion of Ukraine]] on 24 February, environmental issues had almost disappeared from the public.<ref name=":20b">{{Cite web |last=Petrović |first=Ivica |date=17 March 2022 |title=Izborna kampanja u Srbiji u senci rata u Ukrajini |url=https://www.dw.com/sr/izborna-kampanja-u-srbiji-u-senci-rata-u-ukrajini/a-61159223 |access-date=22 March 2022 |website=Deutsche Welle |language=sr-RS}}</ref> CeSID also stated that campaign issues were also concentrated on the fight against corruption and rule of law.<ref name=":20b" /> On the other hand, BIRODI has stated that issues around national interests, economy, and infrastructure were talked about the most.<ref name=":24" /> The organisation also commented that issues regarding European Union integrations had received the smallest amount of coverage.<ref name=":24" />

=== Party campaigns ===
==== Serbian Progressive Party ====
SNS began campaigning shortly after the dissolution of the National Assembly on 15 February.<ref>{{Cite web|date=15 February 2022|title=SNS počeo kampanju: Vučić u Borči potpisao podršku izbornoj listi|url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/vucic-i-sns-poceli-kampanju-skupljaju-potpise-podrske-za-izbornu-listu/|access-date=16 February 2022|website=N1|language=sr-RS}}</ref> It managed to collect around 60,000 signatures that were later submitted to RIK on 16 February, and its ballot list was confirmed a day later.<ref>{{Cite web|date=16 February 2022|title=Predstavnici SNS predali RIK-u preko 58.000 potpisa za listu "Aleksandar Vučić - Zajedno možemo sve"|url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/predstavnici-sns-stigli-u-rik-sa-potpisima-za-listu-aleksandar-vucic-zajedno-mozemo-sve/|access-date=18 February 2022|website=Danas|language=sr-RS}}</ref> Its first campaign rally was held in [[Merošina]].<ref>{{Cite web|date=18 February 2022|title=Vučić sutra u Merošini – prvi predizborni skup SNS|url=https://www.b92.net/info/izbori2022/vesti.php?yyyy=2022&mm=02&dd=18&nav_id=2107307|access-date=18 February 2022|website=B92|language=sr-Latn-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|date=19 February 2022|title=Vučić sa prvog predizbornog skupa narodu poručio: Neće biti gladi, nećemo u NATO|url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/vucic-sa-prvog-predizbornog-skupa-narodu-porucio-nece-biti-gladi-necemo-u-nato/|access-date=19 February 2022|website=N1|language=sr-RS}}</ref> After its first rally, SNS continued its campaign in other regions of Serbia.<ref>{{Cite web |date=26 February 2022 |title=Siniša Mali u Zemunu: Žena je stub svake porodice i svakog društva |url=https://www.b92.net/info/izbori2022/vesti.php?yyyy=2022&mm=02&dd=26&nav_id=2112508 |access-date=3 March 2022 |website=B92 |language=sr-Latn-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=1 March 2022 |title=Danica Grujičić, Milica Nikolić i Krsto Janjušević obišli Moravički okrug |url=https://www.b92.net/info/izbori2022/vesti.php?yyyy=2022&mm=03&dd=01&nav_id=2114242 |access-date=3 March 2022 |website=B92 |language=sr-Latn-RS}}</ref> SNS announced Vučić as its presidential candidate on 6 March.<ref>{{Cite web |date=1 March 2022 |title=Vučić: Odluku o kandidatu donosimo 7. marta |url=https://www.b92.net/info/izbori2022/vesti.php?yyyy=2022&mm=03&dd=01&nav_id=2114100 |access-date=3 March 2022 |website=B92 |language=sr-Latn-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=6 March 2022 |title=Vučić kandidat SNS-a za predsednika Srbije |url=https://www.b92.net/info/izbori2022/vesti.php?yyyy=2022&mm=03&dd=06&nav_id=2116912 |access-date=6 March 2022 |website=B92 |language=sr-Latn-RS}}</ref> After the election, the Agency for Prevention of Corruption stated that Vučić had spent about €6&nbsp;million.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2 July 2022 |title=Prvi među nejednakima: Vučić na kampanju potrošio skoro 14 puta više nego Ponoš |url=https://www.021.rs/story/Info/Srbija/310173/Prvi-medju-nejednakima-Vucic-na-kampanju-potrosio-skoro-14-puta-vise-nego-Ponos.html |access-date=5 July 2022 |website=021.rs |language=sr}}</ref>

==== Socialist Party of Serbia ====
Dačić stated on 16 February that the party had collect more than 20,000 signatures for the parliamentary list.<ref>{{Cite web |title=SPS predala listu za parlamentarne izbore: Skupili više od 20.000 potpisa birača |url=https://www.telegraf.rs/vesti/politika/3459373-sps-predala-listu-za-parlamentarne-izbore-skupili-vise-od-20000-potpisa-biraca |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Telegraf |date=16 February 2022 |language=sr}}</ref> Its list was confirmed by RIK a day later.<ref>{{Cite web |date=17 February 2022 |title=RIK proglasio izbornu listu "Ivica Dačić - Premijer Srbije" |url=https://www.021.rs/story/Info/Srbija/298109/RIK-proglasio-izbornu-listu-Ivica-Dacic-Premijer-Srbije.html |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=021.rs |language=sr}}</ref> SPS has stated its support for Vučić as their joint presidential candidate.<ref>{{Cite web |date=6 March 2022 |title=Lideri SPS-a među prvima dali potpis podrške za kandidaturu Vučića |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/predsednicki-izbori/lideri-sps-a-medju-prvima-dali-potpis-podrske-za-kandidaturu-vucica/ |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=12 March 2022 |title=Dačić: Vučić predsednik, ja premijer |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/dacic-vucic-predsednik-ja-premijer/ |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref> During the campaign, Dačić stated its opposition to [[NATO]] and he expressed support for greater cooperation with China and Russia.<ref>{{Cite web |date=6 March 2022 |title=Dačić: Kosovo i Metohija uvek deo Srbije, ne NATO-u, ne sankcijama Rusiji |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/dacic-kosovo-i-metohija-uvek-deo-srbije-ne-nato-u-ne-sankcijama-rusiji_1320401.html |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=26 February 2022 |title=SPS: Odnosi sa Rusijom i Kinom politički prioritet |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/sps-odnosi-sa-rusijom-i-kinom-politicki-prioritet_1317975.html |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref> SPS had also described itself as a "patriotic party", and during a campaign rally Dačić stated that "SPS equals stability, continuity, and tradition".<ref>{{Cite web |date=25 February 2022 |title=Dačić: Naša politika se nije menjala, SPS jednako patriotizam |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/politika/stranacka-hronika/dacic-nasa-politika-se-nije-menjala-sps-jednako-patriotizam_1317726.html |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=24 February 2022 |title=Dačić: SPS sinonim za državnu stabilnost, tradiciju i trajanje |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/politika/stranacka-hronika/dacic-sps-sinonim-za-drzavnu-stabilnost-tradiciju-i-trajanje_1317391.html |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref> [[Toma Fila]], who was the ballot carrier for the Belgrade City Assembly election, stated his support for [[pensioners' interests]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=27 February 2022 |title=Toma Fila: Najstariji sugrađani su naš prioritet |url=https://nova.rs/vesti/politika/toma-fila-najstariji-sugradjani-su-nas-prioritet/ |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=NOVA portal |language=sr-RS}}</ref> The SPS-led coalition also received support from organisations such as Biogen, Environmental Movement of Beočin, and Democratic Union of Romas.<ref>{{Cite web |date=11 March 2022 |title=Udruženje BIOGEN podržalo listu "IVICA DAČIĆ - PREMIJER SRBIJE": Karić i Rogulja potpisali protokol |url=https://www.kurir.rs/vesti/izbori-2022/3889217/dogovorena-saradnja-udruzenje-biogen-podrzalo-listu-ivica-dacic-premijer-srbije-karic-i-rogulja-potpisali-protokol |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Kurir |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=7 March 2022 |title=Ekološki pokret Beočina podržao listu SPS-JS-Zeleni Srbije |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/ekoloski-pokret-beocina-podrzao-listu-sps-js-zeleni-srbije_1320564.html |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=11 March 2022 |title=Socijalistička partija Srbije i Demokratska unija Roma potpisali sporazum o saradnji |url=http://www.tanjug.rs/full-view.aspx?izb=721737 |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Tanjug |language=sr |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220706204843/http://www.tanjug.rs/full-view.aspx?izb=721737 |archivedate=6 July 2022 |url-status=dead}}</ref> In the first two weeks of the electoral campaign, SPS received US$500,000 in donations for their campaign.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Latković |first=Nataša |date=7 March 2022 |title=Otkrivamo: SPS prikupio skoro pola miliona evra donacija za kampanju |url=https://nova.rs/vesti/politika/otkrivamo-sps-prikupio-skoro-pola-miliona-evra-donacija-za-kampanju/ |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=NOVA portal |language=sr-RS}}</ref>

==== Alliance of Vojvodina Hungarians ====
The [[Alliance of Vojvodina Hungarians]] (VMSZ/SVM) managed to collect around 9,000 signatures, while its ballot list was confirmed on 18 February.<ref>{{Cite web |date=17 February 2022 |title=Savez vojvođanskih Mađara predao listu za parlamentarne izbore |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/savez-vojvodjanskih-madjara-predao-listu-za-parlamentarne-izbore/ |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=18 February 2022 |title=Ko su kandidati Saveza vojvođanskih Mađara-Vajdasági Magyar Szövetség za poslanike |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/ko-su-kandidati-saveza-vojvodjanskih-madjara-vajdasagi-magyar-szovetseg-za-poslanike/ |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref> Its ballot representative [[Bálint Pásztor]] stated that the position of national minorities should be at a higher level. He announced the alliance's support for [[Fidesz]], the ruling party of [[Hungary]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=23 February 2022 |title=Pastor: Ne odustajemo od ambicije da položaj pripadnika nacionalnih manjina bude na visokom nivou |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/pastor-ne-odustajemo-od-ambicije-da-polozaj-pripadnika-nacionalnih-manjina-bude-na-visokom-nivou_1317132.html |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref> Pásztor stated that his party was ready to cooperate with the government to finish multiple projects in [[Subotica]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Jakovljević |first=Natalija |date=25 February 2022 |title=Balint Pastor: U Beograd po pare za sve važne subotičke projekte |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/balint-pastor-u-beograd-po-pare-za-sve-vazne-suboticke-projekte/ |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref> VMSZ stated its support for Vučić for the presidential election.<ref>{{Cite web |date=8 March 2022 |title=SNS predao potpise za kandidaturu Vučića: Cilj istorijska pobeda u prvom krugu |url=https://www.b92.net/info/izbori2022/vesti.php?yyyy=2022&mm=03&dd=08&nav_id=2118061 |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=B92 |language=sr-Latn-RS}}</ref>

==== Serbian Radical Party ====
Over 11,000 signatures were collected by SRS, and their ballot list was confirmed on 18 February.<ref>{{Cite web |date=18 February 2022 |title=Proglašene izborne liste Saveza vojvođanskih Mađara i Srpske radikalne stranke |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/proglasene-izborne-liste-saveza-vojvodjanskih-madjara-i-srpske-radikalne-stranke/ |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref> Šešelj was chosen as the ballot representative; he stated his support for Vučić regarding the presidential election.<ref>{{Cite web |date=5 March 2022 |title=Šešelj u Pirotu: Za Vučića na predsedničkim, za SRS na parlamentarnim izborima |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/seselj-u-pirotu-za-vucica-na-predsednickim-za-srs-na-parlamentarnim-izborima/ |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=8 March 2022 |title=Šešeljevi radikali podržali Vučića za predsednika Srbije |url=https://www.slobodnaevropa.org/a/seselj-vucic-predsednik-kandidatura/31743245.html |access-date=12 March 2022 |newspaper=Radio Slobodna Evropa |language=sr}}</ref> During the campaign, Šešelj stated that the self-proclaimed [[Donetsk People's Republic]] and [[Luhansk People's Republic]] should be recognised by Serbia.<ref>{{Cite web |date=22 February 2022 |title=Šešelj pozdravio priznanje Donjecka i Luganska |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/politika/stranacka-hronika/seselj-pozdravio-priznanje-donjecka-i-luganska_1316626.html |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref> The party also stated its opposition to [[military neutrality]], and that instead stated Serbia should cooperate with Russia and [[BRICS]] countries.<ref>{{Cite web |date=22 February 2022 |title=Aleksandar Šešelj: Licemerno je da Srbija ne prizna teritorijalni integritet Rusije |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/aleksandar-seselj-licemerno-je-da-srbija-ne-prizna-teritorijalni-integritet-rusije_1316790.html |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=12 March 2022 |title=Šešelj: Srbija treba da se okrene Rusiji i Kini |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/seselj-srbija-treba-da-se-okrene-rusiji-i-kini_1322346.html |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref> It also stated that "anti-Serbian [[non-governmental organization]]s" should be banned from being financed.<ref>{{Cite web |date=9 March 2022 |title=Šešelj: Zabranićemo finansiranje NVO koje se bave antisrpskom propagandom |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/seselj-zabranicemo-finansiranje-nvo-koje-se-bave-antisrpskom-propagandom/ |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref> SRS had also noted that [[State aid (European Union)|state aid]] should be provided for domestic economy and agriculture, and that the [[Excise|excise tax]] on fuel for domestic farmers should be abolished.<ref>{{Cite web |date=28 February 2022 |title=Srpski radikali za primat domaće privrede |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/srpski-radikali-za-primat-domace-privrede_1318439.html |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=7 March 2022 |title=SRS: Ukinuti akcize za gorivo domaćim poljoprivrednicima |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/srs-ukinuti-akcize-za-gorivo-domacim-poljoprivrednicima_1320654.html |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref> It had also stated its support for the reform of the Labor Law and its commitment to expanding [[Health care|basic healthcare]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=19 March 2022 |title=Tucaković (SRS): Zakon o radu mora biti promenjen |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/tucakovic-(srs)-zakon-o-radu-mora-biti-promenjen_1324564.html |access-date=21 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=20 March 2022 |title=SRS jedina ima jasnu ideologiju, principe i programski cilj |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/srs-jedina-ima-jasnu-ideologiju-principe-i-programski-cilj_1324745.html |access-date=21 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref>

==== United for the Victory of Serbia ====
The UZPS coalition submitted 13,000 signatures on 18 February and it nominated [[Zdravko Ponoš]] as its presidential candidate.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2 February 2022 |title=Predstavljanje kandidata dela opozicije - govore Tepić, Janković i Ponoš |url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/predstavljanje-kandidata-dela-opozicije-govore-tepic-jankovic-i-ponos/ |access-date=29 September 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=18 February 2022 |title=Opoziciona koalicija Ujedinjena Srbija podnela listu za parlamentarne izbore |url=https://www.slobodnaevropa.org/a/srbija-izbori-opozicija/31710042.html |access-date=29 September 2022 |newspaper=Radio Slobodna Evropa |language=sr}}</ref> Its campaign began on 22 February, while its last campaign rally was held on 31 March.<ref>{{Cite web |date=22 February 2022 |title=Ujedinjena Srbija počela kampanju iz Niša: Olovkom do pobede 3. aprila |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/ujedinjena-srbija-pocela-kampanju-iz-nisa-olovkom-do-pobede-3-aprila/ |access-date=29 September 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=31 March 2022 |title=Tepić: Većinska Srbija ne želi Vučića, ali mora to da pokaže u nedelju |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/tepic-vecinska-srbija-ne-zeli-vucica-ali-mora-to-da-pokaze-u-nedelju/ |access-date=29 September 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref> UZPS campaigned on the formation of technocratic teams and an anti-corruption body, and it voiced support for lustration, transparency, and social justice.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Nešić |first=Nenad |date=2 February 2022 |title=Izborna priča kreće: "Ujedinili se general, diplomata i najhrabrija političarka" |url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/izborna-prica-krece-ujedinili-se-general-diplomata-i-najhrabrija-politicarka/ |access-date=29 September 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2 February 2022 |title=Opozicija predstavila kandidate za predsednika, gradonačelnika i nosioca liste |url=http://www.rts.rs/page/stories/sr/story/9/politika/4686216/opozicija-kandidati.html |access-date=29 September 2022 |website=Radio Television of Serbia |language=sr}}</ref>

==== National Democratic Alternative ====
NADA submitted 12,000 signatures on 19 February and nominated [[Miloš Jovanović]] as its presidential candidate.<ref>{{Cite web |date=6 February 2022 |title=Koalicija NADA: Miloš Jovanović kandidat za predsednika |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/koalicija-nada-milos-jovanovic-kandidat-za-predsednika/ |access-date=29 September 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=19 February 2022 |title=Koalicija NADA predala listu za parlamentarne izbore |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/koalicija-nada-predala-listu-za-parlamentarne-izbore/ |access-date=29 September 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref> NADA campaigned against imposing sanctions on Russia.<ref>{{Cite web |date=30 March 2022 |title=Jovanović: Koalicija NADA ponudila konkretna rešenja problema |url=https://www.euronews.rs/izbori-2022/vesti/42924/jovanovic-koalicija-nada-ponudila-konkretna-resenja-problema/vest |access-date=29 September 2022 |website=Euronews |language=sr}}</ref>

==== Serbian Party Oathkeepers ====
SSZ had their parliamentary list confirmed by RIK on 20 February, with [[Milica Đurđević Stamenkovski]] as its ballot representative.<ref>{{Cite web |date=20 February 2022 |title=Ko su kandidati za poslanike Srpske stranke Zavetnici? |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/ko-su-kandidati-za-poslanike-srpske-stranke-zavetnici/ |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref> SSZ also nominated Đurđević Stamenkovski as its presidential candidate in early February 2022, while RIK confirmed her candidacy on 8 March, shortly after the proclamation of the presidential electoral campaign.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Radovanović |first=Vojin |date=6 February 2022 |title=Zavetnici odlučili: Milica Đurđević Stamenkovski kandidat za predsednika |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/zavetnici-odlucili-milica-djurdjevic-stamenkovski-kandidat-za-predsednika/ |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=8 March 2022 |title=RIK proglasio Đurđević Stamenkovski za predsedničkog kandidata |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/rik-proglasio-djurdjevic-stamenkovski-za-predsednickog-kandidata/ |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref> Representatives of the party orchestrated a protest on 4 March following the ban of Russian government-owned [[RT (TV network)|RT]] channel in Europe.<ref>{{Cite web |date=22 April 2022 |title=Zavetnici protiv suzbijanja slobode govora u EU |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/zavetnici-protiv-suzbijanja-slobode-govora-u-eu_1319910.html |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref> Đurđević Stamenkovski had also stated that Serbia should establish closer ties with Russia.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2 March 2022 |title=Deo opozicije osudio glasanje Srbije za rezoluciju UN o Rusiji |url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/zavetnici-vlast-podlegla-pritiscima-sledeci-korak-sankcije-rusiji/ |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=22 February 2022 |title=Milica Đurđević: Srbija da ne uvodi sankcije Rusiji |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/milica-djurdjevic-srbija-da-ne-uvodi-sankcije-rusiji/ |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref>

==== Justice and Reconciliation Party ====
[[File:Muftijin Amanet logo.svg|thumb|upright=0.7|Logo of the Justice and Reconciliation Party's electoral campaign]]
The [[Justice and Reconciliation Party]] (SPP), led by [[Usame Zukorlić]], submitted its ballot list on 19 February, while RIK confirmed the ballot a day later, with 5,056 valid signatures.<ref>{{Cite web |date=20 February 2022 |title=Proglašene izborne liste Zavetnika i Stranke pravde i pomirenja |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/proglasene-izborne-liste-zavetnika-i-stranke-pravde-i-pomirenja/ |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref> On 7 March, Zukorlić stated that he would expect the cooperation between SPP and SNS to continue after the election.<ref>{{Cite web |date=7 March 2022 |title=Zukorlić: Očekujemo nastavak saradnje sa SNS |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/zukrolic-ocekujemo-nastavak-saradnje-sa-sns/ |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref> During the electoral campaign, the party expressed its support to have as many women as possible in management positions, as well as the affirmation of women's entrepreneurship.<ref>{{Cite web |date=6 March 2022 |title=SPP: Da što više žena bude na rukovodećim pozicijama |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/politika/stranacka-hronika/spp-da-sto-vise-zena-bude-na-rukovodecim-pozicijama_1320355.html |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref> The party had also stated its support for reconciliation, [[education reform]]s and [[anti-discrimination]] politics.<ref>{{Cite web |date=9 March 2022 |title=SPP: Politika pomirenja ključna za razvoj Srbije |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/spp-politika-pomirenja-kljucna-za-razvoj-srbije_1321493.html |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=7 March 2022 |title=Demić (SPP): Jedan od ciljeva unapređenje obrazovanja |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/demic-(spp)-jedan-od-ciljeva-unapredjenje-obrazovanja_1320697.html |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=1 March 2022 |title=Poštovanje prava žena i dece: Poruka izborne liste "Muftijin amanet" |url=https://www.novosti.rs/vesti/izbori-2022/1091435/postovanje-prava-zena-dece-poruka-izborne-liste-muftijin-amanet |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Novosti |language=sr}}</ref> In late March, the party endorsed Vučić.<ref>{{Cite web |date=29 March 2022 |title=Stranka pravde i pomirenja podržava Vučića na predsedničkim izborima |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/predsednicki-izbori/stranka-pravde-i-pomirenja-podrzava-vucica-na-predsednickim-izborima/ |access-date=1 April 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref>

==== We Must ====
The We Must coalition submitted its signatures on 21 February.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Petković |first=Gordana |date=21 February 2022 |title=Koalicija "Moramo" predala listu za parlamentarne i beogradske izbore |url=https://nova.rs/vesti/politika/koalicija-moramo-predala-listu-za-parlamentarne-i-gradske-izbore/ |access-date=29 September 2022 |website=NOVA portal |language=sr}}</ref> Its first campaign rally was held on 27 February, during which it announced [[Biljana Stojković]] as its presidential candidate.<ref>{{Cite web |date=27 February 2022 |title=Biljana Stojković predsednička kandidatkinja SSS i koalicije Moramo |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/predsednicki-izbori/biljana-stojkovic-predsednicka-kandidatkinja-sss-i-koalicije-moramo/ |access-date=29 September 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref> During the campaign period, the We Must coalition received support from German [[The Left (Germany)|The Left]], Danish [[Red–Green Alliance (Denmark)|Red–Green Alliance]], and Slovenian [[The Left (Slovenia)|The Left]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=31 March 2022 |title=Međunarodna podrška levice koaliciji Moramo |url=https://solidarnost.net/medjunarodna-podrska-levice-koaliciji-moramo/ |access-date=29 September 2022 |website=Solidarnost |language=sr-RS}}</ref>

==== Sovereignists ====
The Sovereignists coalition chose [[Saša Radulović]] as the ballot representative.<ref>{{Cite web |date=23 February 2022 |title=Proglašena izborna lista "Suverenisti" |url=https://www.021.rs/story/Info/Srbija/298585/Proglasena-izborna-lista-Suverenisti.html |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=www.021.rs |language=sr}}</ref> The coalition announced [[Branka Stamenković]] as its presidential candidate on 28 February.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Popović |first=Sofija |date=1 March 2022 |title=Predsednička kandidatkinja Branka Stamenković: Kraljica retrogradnog Merkura |url=https://www.vreme.com/vesti/predsednicka-kandidatkinja-branka-stamenkovic-kraljica-retrogradnog-merkura/ |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Vreme |language=sr-RS}}</ref> One of the representatives of the coalition, [[Milan Stamatović]], stated that "Serbia should not impose sanctions on Russia", while Radulović stated that "it is unfortunate that Serbia sided with NATO" during the Russian invasion of Ukraine.<ref>{{Cite web |date=25 February 2022 |title=Stamatović: Srbija nikada ne sme da uvede sankcije Rusiji |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/stamatovic-srbija-nikada-ne-sme-da-uvede-sankcije-rusiji_1317742.html |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=3 March 2022 |title=Radulović: Za žaljenje je što je Srbija stala na stranu NATO |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/radulovic-za-zaljenje-je-sto-je-srbija-stala-na-stranu-nato/ |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref> During the campaign, Radulović stated the coalition's support for "[[Souverainism|souverainist]] policies" and its opposition to mandatory vaccination.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2 March 2022 |title=Radulović: Suverenizam protiv globalizma |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/politika/stranacka-hronika/radulovic-suverenizam-protiv-globalizma_1319220.html |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=7 March 2022 |title=Koalicija Suverenisti: Vakcinacija treba da je dobrovoljna |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/koalicija-suverenisti-vakcinacija-treba-da-je-dobrovoljna_1320693.html |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref> The Sovereignists stated their support for implementing [[blockchain]] technology and free textbooks for [[kindergarten]]s and [[primary school]]s.<ref>{{Cite web |date=5 March 2022 |title=Radulović: Reformisaćemo državnu upravu blokčejn tehnologijom |url=https://nova.rs/vesti/politika/radulovic-reformisacemo-drzavnu-upravu-blokcejn-tehnologijom/ |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=NOVA portal |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=8 March 2022 |title=Radulović (Suverenisti): Država da obezbedi besplatne udžbenike i vrtiće za svu decu |url=https://beta.rs/vesti/politika-vesti-srbija/160076-radulovic-suverenisti-drzava-da-obezbedi-besplatne-udzbenike-i-vrtice-za-svu-decu |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Novinska agencija Beta |language=sr |archive-date=8 March 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220308131657/https://beta.rs/vesti/politika-vesti-srbija/160076-radulovic-suverenisti-drzava-da-obezbedi-besplatne-udzbenike-i-vrtice-za-svu-decu |url-status=dead }}</ref> During an interview, Stamenković stated her support for the introduction of [[mandatory conscription]] into the army.<ref>{{Cite web |date=21 March 2022 |title=Predsednička kandidatkinja liste "Suverenisti" Branka Stamenković |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/predsednicki-izbori/predsednicka-kandidatkinja-liste-%E2%80%9Csuverenisti-branka-stamenkovic_1325137.html |access-date=21 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref>

==== Dveri–POKS ====
Dveri announced its participation in the upcoming elections under the "Patriotic Bloc", which was formed in December 2021.<ref name=":2" /> It opposed the legalisation of civil unions,<ref>{{cite web|date=16 May 2021|title=Utisak nedelje: Kome smetaju istopolne zajednice|url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/utisak-nedelje-kome-smetaju-istopolne-zajednice/|access-date=30 January 2022|website=N1|language=sr}}</ref> and the coalition has expressed their support towards [[monarchism]], [[Right-wing antiglobalism|antiglobalism]], and abolition of [[Vaccine passports during the COVID-19 pandemic|vaccine passports]].<ref>{{Cite web|last=Popović|first=Sofija|date=2 February 2022|title=Predsednički kandidat Boško Obradović: Pravoslavni rodoljub|url=https://www.vreme.com/vesti/predsednicki-kandidat-bosko-obradovic-bogobojazljiv-rodoljub/|access-date=9 February 2022|website=Vreme|language=sr-RS}}</ref> Its leader, [[Boško Obradović]], was chosen as their presidential candidate in January 2022.<ref>{{Cite web|date=27 January 2022|title=Obradović zvanično kandidat, Dveri u kampanji pod sloganom "Srcem za Srbiju"|url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/obradovic-zvanicno-kandidat-dveri-u-kampanji-pod-sloganom-srcem-za-srbiju/|access-date=9 February 2022|website=Danas|language=sr-RS}}</ref> Obradović had also participated in talks regarding the formation of a united "Patriotic bloc" that would also include other right-leaning parties, although the talks had stalled shortly after.<ref>{{Cite web|title=DESNICA SE UJEDINJUJE ZA IZBORE? Zavetnici, Dveri, DSS, DJB i POKS danas na sastanku, moguć i zajednički predsednički kandidat|url=https://www.blic.rs/vesti/politika/desnica-se-ujedinjuje-za-izbore-zavetnici-dveri-dss-djb-i-poks-danas-na-sastanku/f69596p|access-date=9 February 2022|website=Blic.rs|date=7 February 2022 |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Nema dogovora oko zajedničkog predsedničkog kandidata patriotskog bloka?|url=https://www.b92.net/info/vesti/index.php?yyyy=2022&mm=02&dd=09&nav_category=11&nav_id=2102494|access-date=9 February 2022|website=B92.net|language=sr}}</ref> Dveri leadership announced their support for a joint "patriotic ballot list" on 13 February.<ref>{{Cite web|date=13 February 2022|title=Dveri: Glavni odbor podržao jedinstvenu opozicionu patriotsku izbornu listu|url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/dveri-glavni-odbor-podrzao-jedinstvenu-opozicionu-patriotsku-izbornu-listu/|access-date=13 February 2022|website=N1|language=sr-RS}} {{Dead link|date=September 2026 |bot=InternetArchiveBot }}</ref> Obradović announced on 16 February that Dveri reached an agreement with Gojković-led POKS faction to participate in a joint list.<ref>{{Cite web|date=16 February 2022|title=Boško Obradović i Žika Gojković potpisali koalicioni sporazum|url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/bosko-obradovic-i-zika-gojkovic-potpisali-koalicioni-sporazum/|access-date=16 February 2022|website=N1|language=sr-RS}}</ref> Soon after, [[Slobodan Samardžić]] and Duško Kuzović left the coalition.<ref>{{Cite web|date=16 February 2022|title=Državotvorni pokret Srbije istupio iz bloka oko Dveri|url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/drzavotvorni-pokret-srbije-istupio-iz-bloka-oko-dveri/|access-date=16 February 2022|website=N1|language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Profesor Kuzović napustio Patriotski blok {{!}} Izbori 2022|url=https://direktno.rs/izbori-2022/398817/dusko-kuzovic-patriotski-blok-bosko-obradovic-poks-zika-gojkovic.html|access-date=20 February 2022|website=Direktno|language=sr}}</ref> Obradović stated that his campaign would be mainly focused on the restoration of the monarchy.<ref>{{Cite web|date=18 February 2022|title=Obradović: Moja kandidatura se bazira na ideji vraćanja monarhističkog uređenja|url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/predsednicki-izbori/obradovic-moja-kandidatura-se-bazira-na-ideji-vracanja-monarhistickog-uredjenja/|access-date=18 February 2022|website=N1|language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=28 March 2022 |title=Predsednički kandidat Boško Obradović: Vratićemo monarhiju u Srbiju |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/predsednicki-izbori/predsednicki-kandidat-bosko-obradovic-vraticemo-monarhiju-u-srbiju_1327324.html |access-date=29 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref> The coalition had received support from pulmonologist Branimir Nestorović.<ref>{{Cite web |date=25 March 2022 |title=Branimir Nestorović podržao Patriotski blok |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/politika/stranacka-hronika/branimir-nestorovic-podrzao-patriotski-blok_1326618.html |access-date=27 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref>

Its parliamentary list was confirmed by RIK on 23 February.<ref>{{Cite web |date=23 February 2022 |title=RIK proglasio izbornu listu Dveri i frakcije POKS-a koju predvodi Žika Gojković |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/rik-proglasio-izbornu-listu-dveri-i-frakcije-poks-a-koju-predvodi-zika-gojkovic/ |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref> During the campaign, Obradović stated that one of the coalition's priorities is to enforce [[Economic nationalism|economic patriotism]] and to raise conditions for villagers and farmers.<ref>{{Cite web |date=4 March 2022 |title=Obradović: Pomoć domaćoj privredi prioritet Patriotskog bloka |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/obradovic-pomoc-domacoj-privredi-prioritet-patriotskog-bloka_1319902.html |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=11 March 2022 |title=Dveri: Jako selo za jaku državu |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/dveri-jako-selo-za-jaku-drzavu_1322174.html |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref> [[Miloš Parandilović]], the ballot representative, said that the Dveri–POKS coalition is supportive of breaking up [[Monopoly|monopolies]] and to fight against [[crime]] and [[corruption]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=7 March 2022 |title=Parandilović: Prioritet primena Zakona o utvrđivanju imovine |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/parandilovic-prioritet-primena-zakona-o-utvrdjivanju-imovine_1320752.html |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref> It had also stated its opposition to NATO.<ref>{{Cite web |date=10 March 2022 |title=Dveri: Protiv članstva u NATO |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/dveri-protiv-clanstva-u-nato_1321790.html |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref>

==== Vojvodinians ====
The Vojvodinians coalition, which is led by the [[Democratic Alliance of Croats in Vojvodina]] (DSHV) and [[Together for Vojvodina (party)|Together for Vojvodina]], a political party with ties to the [[League of Social Democrats of Vojvodina]] (LSV),<ref name=":23">{{cite web |date=2 March 2022 |title=RIK proglasio manjinsku izbornu listu Zajedno za Vojvodinu |url=http://www.rts.rs/page/stories/sr/Izbori2022/story/3387/izborne-komisije/4722784/rik-proglasenje-lista-zajedno-za-vojvodinu.html |access-date=15 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Serbia |language=sr}}</ref> submitted its ballot on 1 March.<ref>{{cite web |date=1 March 2022 |title=DSHV i koalicija "Vojvođani" predali listu kandidata za izbore u Srbiji |url=https://www.glasistre.hr/svijet/dshv-i-koalicija-vojvodani-predali-listu-kandidata-za-izbore-u-srbiji-780381 |access-date=15 March 2022 |website=Glas Istre |language=hr}}</ref> The ballot list was confirmed by RIK a day later.<ref name=":23" /> LSV had also publicly stated its support for the coalition.<ref>{{cite web |date=27 March 2022 |title=LSV: Vratiti u parlament autentične predstavnike Vojvodine |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/lsv-vratiti-u-parlament-autenticne-predstavnike-vojvodine_1318145.html |access-date=15 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref>

The coalition had primarily campaigned on "bringing Vojvodina back to the National Assembly".<ref>{{Cite web |date=7 March 2022 |title=Vojvođani: Za poslanike one kojima je stalo do Vojvodine |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/vojvodjani-za-poslanike-one-kojima-je-stalo-do-vojvodine_1320777.html |access-date=15 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref><ref name=":21">{{cite web |date=11 March 2022 |title=Žigmanov: Došlo je vreme da se Vojvođani vrate u parlament |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/zigmanov-doslo-je-vreme-da-se-vojvodjani-vrate-u-parlament/ |access-date=15 March 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref> It had also stated its support for [[Progressivism|progressive]] policies and fiscal decentralisation,<ref name=":21" /><ref>{{cite web |date=13 March 2022 |title=Mrnuštik: Vojvodini potreban decentralizovani poreski sistem |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/mrnustik-vojvodini-potreban-decentralizovani-poreski-sistem_1322557.html |access-date=15 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref> and its opposition to "cutting Vojvodina's forests" and "dirty technologies".<ref>{{cite web |date=8 March 2022 |title=Olenik (Vojvođani): Borićemo se protiv seča šuma |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/olenik-(vojvodjani)-boricemo-se-protiv-seca-suma_1321078.html |access-date=15 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref> [[Tomislav Žigmanov]], the coalition representative, had also stated their support for Serbia to join the European Union and NATO.<ref>{{Cite web |date=11 March 2022 |title=Žigmanov: Pripadnici hrvatske zajednice da se na popisu izjasne kao Hrvati - pripadnici regije Vojvodina |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/zigmanov-pripadnici-hrvatske-zajednice-da-se-na-popisu-izjasne-kao-hrvati-pripadnici-regije-vojvodina_1322268.html |access-date=15 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=14 March 2022 |title=Žigmanov: Želimo da vidimo Vojvodinu u EU i NATO paktu |url=https://www.021.rs/story/Info/Vojvodina/300227/Zigmanov-Zelimo-da-vidimo-Vojvodinu-u-EU-i-NATO-paktu.html |access-date=15 March 2022 |website=021.rs |language=sr}}</ref> The coalition began campaigning on 10 March, and during their first rally in [[Subotica]], the coalition had also expressed their support towards [[multiculturalism]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=10 March 2022 |title=Koalicija Zajedno za Vojvodinu - Vojvođani u Subotici: Da se Vojvodina vrati u parlament |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/koalicija-zajedno-za-vojvodinu-vojvodjani-u-subotici-da-se-vojvodina-vrati-u-parlament/ |access-date=15 March 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=11 March 2022 |title=Predstavljena koalicija Zajedno za Vojvodinu-Vojvođani |url=https://www.subotica.com/vesti/predstavljena-koalicija-zajedno-za-vojvodinu-vojvodjani-id43675.html |access-date=15 March 2022 |website=Subotica.com |language=sr-Latn}}</ref>

==== SDS–Nova ====
The coalition led by SDS and Nova ballot list was confirmed by RIK on 8 March.<ref>{{Cite web |date=8 March 2022 |title=Ko su kandidati za poslanike na listi Boris Tadić-Ajmo ljudi |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/ko-su-kandidati-za-poslanike-na-listi-boris-tadic-ajmo-ljudi/ |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref> SDS announced Dragoslav Šumarac as its presidential candidate on 12 March, although Šumarac withdrew his candidature a day later after not receiving support from his coalition partners.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Radovanović |first=Vojin |date=12 March 2022 |title=Predsednički kandidat Tadićeve SDS Dragoslav Šumarac za sad bez podrške Nove i 1od5miliona |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/predsednicki-kandidat-sds-dragoslav-sumarac/ |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=13 March 2022 |title=Dragoslav Šumarac povlači kandidaturu za predsednika Srbije |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/predsednicki-izbori/dragoslav-sumarac-povlaci-kandidaturu-za-predsednika-srbije/ |access-date=13 March 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref> During the campaign, the coalition stated its support for adopting a long-term strategy regarding agricultural development.<ref>{{Cite web |date=8 March 2022 |title=Radosavljević: Treba nam dugoročna strategija poljoprivrede |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/radosavljevic-treba-nam-dugorocna-strategija-poljoprivrede_1321022.html |access-date=12 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref> It had also expressed its support towards the accession of Serbia to the European Union, although it also stated its opposition to sanction Russia.<ref>{{Cite web |date=8 March 2022 |title=Predizborni razgovori na RTV-u: Predstavnici Tadićeve koalicije protiv uvođenja sankcija Rusiji |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/predizborni-razgovori-na-rtv-u-predstavnici-tadiceve-koalicije-protiv-uvodjenja-sankcija-rusiji_1321179.html |access-date=13 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref>

==== Others ====
[[File:Миша Вацић билборд.png|thumb|upright=0.6|alt=A billboard featuring Miša Vacić|A billboard featuring Miša Vacić]]
The SDAS ballot list was confirmed on 2 March, with around 7,000 valid signatures.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2 March 2022 |title=RIK proglasio listu SDA Sandžaka |url=https://sandzakpress.net/rik-proglasio-listu-sda-sandzaka-2/ |access-date=13 March 2022 |website=Sandžak Press |language=bs-BA}}</ref> Its first campaign rally was held in [[Novi Pazar]] on 9 March.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Ličina |first=Irfan |date=9 March 2022 |title="Srpski narod je postigao imunitet na velikosrpski virus koji je širio režim" |url=https://nova.rs/izbori-2022/sulejman-ugljanin-velikosrpski-virus/ |access-date=13 March 2022 |website=NOVA portal |language=sr-RS}}</ref> The civic group "Stolen Babies", which is led by Ana Pejić, stated their opposition to [[Human trafficking|baby trafficking]] during an interview on 16 March.<ref>{{Cite web |date=16 March 2022 |title=Grupa građana "Otete bebe": Cilj nam je rešavanje bebi afere i stavljanje u fokus problema malog običnog čoveka |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/grupa-gradjana-otete-bebe-cilj-nam-je-resavanje-bebi-afere-i-stavljanje-u-fokus-problema-malog-obicnog-coveka_1323763.html |access-date=21 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref> [[Srđan Šajn]], the leader of the [[Roma Party]], stated his support for [[labour rights]] and his opposition to "unfair [[privatization]]".<ref>{{Cite web |date=21 March 2022 |title=Romska partija protiv "džipsi industrije", za radničku Srbiju |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/romska-partija-protiv-dzipsi-industrije-za-radnicku-srbiju_1325075.html |access-date=21 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=25 March 2022 |title=Šajn o nepravednoj privatizaciji |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/sajn-o-nepravednoj-privatizaciji_1326363.html |access-date=27 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref> Presidential candidate [[Miša Vacić]] expressed his support for introducing mandatory conscription and increasing the rights for [[Veteran|war veterans]] in Serbia.<ref>{{Cite web |date=18 March 2022 |title=Vacić: Kao predsednik boriću se za vraćanje vojnog roka |url=https://www.rtv.rs/sr_lat/izbori-2022/predsednicki-izbori/vacic-kao-predsednik-boricu-se-za-vracanje-vojnog-roka_1324325.html |access-date=21 March 2022 |website=Radio Television of Vojvodina |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=21 March 2022 |title=Miša Vacić: Pobrinuću se za ostvarivanje prava svih ratnih veterana Srbije |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/predsednicki-izbori/misa-vacic-pobrinucu-se-za-ostvarivanje-prava-svih-ratnih-veterana-srbije/ |access-date=21 March 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref> The Russian Minority Alliance, which was primarily led by the [[neo-fascist]] [[Leviathan Movement]], was initially rejected by RIK, although after the case got overturned by the Constitutional Court, RIK confirmed their ballot.<ref name=":20">{{Cite web |date=16 March 2022 |title=Pojedine stranke glume manjine da bi lakše "uskočile" u poslaničke klupe |url=https://www.021.rs/story/Info/Srbija/300348/Pojedine-stranke-glume-manjine-da-bi-lakse-uskocile-u-poslanicke-klupe.html |access-date=27 March 2022 |website=021.rs |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=22 March 2022 |title=Ruski manjinski savez biće 19. lista za narodne poslanike, počinje štampanje glasačkih listića |url=https://www.021.rs/story/Info/Srbija/300907/Ruski-manjinski-savez-bice-19-lista-za-narodne-poslanike-pocinje-stampanje-glasackih-listica.html |access-date=27 March 2022 |website=021.rs |language=sr}}</ref> CeSID claimed that the ballot list did not represent minority rights but [[far-right politics]], while CRTA claimed that they had falsified the signatures.<ref name=":20" /><ref>{{Cite web |date=24 March 2022 |title=Crta: Hitno ispitati navode o falsifikovanju potpisa za Ruski manjinski savez |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/crta-hitno-ispitati-navode-o-falsifikovanju-potpisa-za-ruski-manjinski-savez/ |access-date=27 March 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref>

