== Results ==
Voting stations were opened from 07:00 ([[Central European Time|UTC+01:00]]) to 20:00, and there were 6,502,307 citizens in total that had the right to vote in the general elections.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Miletić |first=Miljana |date=2 February 2022 |title=Kako pravilno glasati i šta štiti prava birača u Srbiji |url=https://www.slobodnaevropa.org/a/izbori-srbija-glasanje-glasaci-prava-zakon/31779750.html |access-date=3 April 2022 |website=Radio Free Europe |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=1 April 2022 |title=RIK: U Srbiji 6.502.307 birača |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/rik-u-srbiji-6-502-307-biraca/ |access-date=3 April 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref> According to preliminary results that were published by CRTA and Ipsos/CeSID, Vučić won in the first round of the presidential elections, although SNS also lost its majority status in the National Assembly according to the parliamentary election results.<ref>{{Cite web |date=4 March 2022 |title=Pobeda Vučića i SNS, Beograd još enigma |url=https://www.dw.com/sr/izbori2022%EF%B8%8F-pobeda-vu%C4%8Di%C4%87a-i-sns-beograd-jo%C5%A1-enigma/a-61342446 |access-date=3 April 2022 |website=Deutsche Welle |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=3 April 2022 |title=IPSOS/CeSID: Prvi preliminarni rezultati parlamentarnih izbora |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/ipsos-cesid-prvi-preliminarni-rezultati-parlamentarnih-izbora/ |access-date=3 April 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=3 April 2022 |title=Preliminarni rezultati predsedničkih izbora u Srbiji 2022. najnovije vesti |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/predsednicki-izbori/preliminarni-rezultati-predsednickih-izbora-u-srbiji-2022-najnovije-vesti/ |access-date=3 April 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref> In diaspora, Vučić won more votes than Ponoš.<ref>{{Cite web |date=7 April 2022 |title=RIK: Vučić u inostranstvu dobio 20.198, Ponoš 5.955 glasova |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/predsednicki-izbori/rik-vucic-u-inostranstvu-dobio-20-198-ponos-5-955-glasova/ |access-date=7 April 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Cvejić |first=B. |date=6 April 2022 |title=Kako je glasala dijaspora: Vučić pobedio u Beču, Berlinu, Moskvi, Ponoš u Londonu, Briselu, Stokholmu |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/kako-je-glasala-dijaspora-vucic-pobedio-u-becu-berlinu-moskvi-ponos-u-londonu-briselu-stokholmu/ |access-date=7 April 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref> SNS managed to strengthen its presence in suburban and rural areas, although it underperformed in major cities such as [[Belgrade]], [[Novi Sad]], [[Niš]], and [[Valjevo]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bogosavljević |first=Žarko |date=5 April 2022 |title=Velika analiza: Kako je glasao Novi Sad - koliko ima SNS, a koliko opozicija |url=https://www.021.rs/story/Novi-Sad/Vesti/302133/Velika-analiza-Kako-je-glasao-Novi-Sad-koliko-ima-SNS-a-koliko-opozicija.html |access-date=13 April 2022 |website=021.rs |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last1=Tasić |first1=T. |last2=Radovanović |first2=T. |date=5 April 2022 |title=I u Nišu Vučić ubedljivo pobedio, na parlamentarnim izborima za SNS oko 37% |url=https://www.juznevesti.com/Politika/I-u-Nisu-Vucic-ubedljivo-pobedio-na-parlamentarnim-izborima-za-SNS-oko-37.sr.html |access-date=13 April 2022 |website=Južne vesti |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Kuzmanović |first=Milena |date=4 April 2022 |title=SNS osvojila u Valjevu 34,77 odsto glasova |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/sns-osvojila-u-valjevu-3477-odsto-glasova/ |access-date=13 April 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref>

RIK announced that voting would be repeated at some stations where the results could not be determined, effectively postponing the announcement of final results.<ref>{{Cite web |date=6 April 2022 |title=RIK: Odlaže se objavljivanje konačnih rezultata zbog ponavljanja glasanja |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/rik-odlaze-se-objavljivanje-konacnih-rezultata-zbog-ponavljanja-glasanja/ |access-date=6 April 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=6 April 2022 |title=RIK: Ponovljeno glasanje za parlamentarne i predsedničke izbore 16. aprila |url=https://n1info.rs/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/rik-ponovljeno-glasanje-za-parlamentarne-izbore-u-subotu-16-aprila/ |access-date=18 January 2023 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref> Voting was repeated five times; on 16 and 28 April, on 27 May, and on 23 and 30 June.<ref>{{Cite web |date=7 April 2022 |title=RIK: Ponovno glasanje na pojedinim biračkim mestima biće održano 16. aprila |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/rik-na-nekim-mestima-ponovljeno-glasanje-na-predsednickim-izborima-u-subotu-16-aprila/ |access-date=7 April 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref name="RIKLive">{{Cite web |title=Prenos uživo |url=https://www.rik.parlament.gov.rs/tekst/284079/prenos-uzivo.php |access-date=4 April 2022 |website=Republic Electoral Commission |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=28 April 2022 |title=Kamberi će biti poslanik u Skupštini Srbije |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/kamberi-ce-biti-poslanik-u-skupstini-srbije/ |access-date=29 April 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref> The [[Albanian Coalition of Preševo Valley]] (KSLP) initially gained a seat following the 28 April repeat election, although following the repeat election on 27 May, it lost its seat to SPS; the coalition only needed 12 more votes to retain its seat in the National Assembly.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Stojanović |first=Milan |date=27 May 2022 |title=Albanci ipak bez poslanika u Skupštini Srbije, nedostajalo im 12 glasova |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/albanci-ipak-bez-poslanika-u-skupstini-nezvanicno-nedostaje-im-11-glasova/ |access-date=28 May 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref> The Administrative Court rejected the results of repeated elections that were held on 27 May, and the fourth repeated election in [[Veliki Trnovac]] was set to be held on 23 June.<ref>{{Cite web |date=17 June 2022 |title=Parlamentarni izbori u Velikom Trnovcu: Nastaviće se |url=https://www.vreme.com/vesti/parlamentarni-izbori-u-velikom-trnovcu-nastavice-se/ |access-date=18 June 2022 |website=Vreme |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref name=":26">{{Cite web |date=17 June 2022 |title=Nova vlada sve dalja: Upravni sud ponovo poništio izbore u Velikom Trnovcu |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/ponavljanje-izbora-veliki-trnovac/ |access-date=18 June 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref> On the day of the election, the voting station in Veliki Trnovac did not open on time and members of the polling station committee did not agree on the division of roles. Additionally, a [[bomb threat]] was reported at the voting station, and because of it the election was postponed. RIK announced that the election would be repeated again on 30 June.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bjeletić |first=Gordana |date=23 June 2022 |title=Četvrti put - ništa: Nema glasanja u Velikom Trnovcu danas |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/jos-nije-pocelo-glasanje-u-velikom-trnovcu/ |access-date=23 June 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=23 June 2022 |title=Veliki Trnovac: Moguće je da će glasati i peti put |url=https://www.vreme.com/vesti/veliki-trnovac-moguce-je-da-ce-glasati-i-peti-put/ |access-date=23 June 2022 |website=Vreme |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=24 June 2022 |title=RIK donosi odluku da se u Velikom Trnovcu ponovo glasa 30. juna |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/parlamentarni-izbori/izbori-u-velikom-trnovcu/ |access-date=24 June 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS |last=Kojić |first=Nikola}}</ref> In the fifth repeat election, KSLP won enough votes to retain its only seat in the National Assembly.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Ristić |first=V. |date=30 June 2022 |title=U Velikom Trnovcu najviše glasova osvojila lista "Koalicija Albanaca Doline": Kamberiju novi mandat u Skupštini Srbije |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/kamberiju-novi-mandat-u-skupstini-srbije/ |access-date=1 July 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |title=Albancima mesto u Skupštini Srbije, kažu prvi rezultati ponovljenih izbora u Velikom Trnovcu |url=https://www.slobodnaevropa.org/a/izbori-peti-pu-veliki-trnovac/31922754.html |access-date=1 July 2022 |newspaper=Radio Slobodna Evropa |date=July 2022 |language=sr}}</ref>

Many crowds formed in polling stations across Serbia, mostly due to the simultaneous holding of elections at several levels, which slowed down the process, but also because of increased voter turnout.<ref>{{Cite web |date=3 April 2022 |title=CRTA: Gužve na biračkim mestima, glasanje veoma sporo zbog izbora na više nivoa |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/crta-do-13-sati-je-na-izbore-izaslo-267-odsto-gradjana/ |access-date=3 April 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr}}</ref> In the end, the turnout was reported to be at around 59%, making it the largest turnout since the [[2008 Serbian parliamentary election|2008 elections]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=3 April 2022 |title=Izbori 2022: Vučić pobedio u prvom krugu, opozicija se nada vlasti u Beogradu |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/izbori-u-srbiji/ |access-date=7 April 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref>

