== Aftermath ==
[[File:Protests in front of RIK, 4 April 2022.png|thumb|upright=0.8|alt=A protest in front of the building of RIK a day after the elections|A protest in front of the building of RIK a day after the elections]]
CeSID reported that electoral irregularities occurred in the early hours of the election.<ref>{{Cite web |date=3 April 2022 |title=CeSid: Zabeležene različite nepravilnosti na biračkim mestima |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/cesid-zabelezene-razlicite-nepravilnosti-na-birackim-mestima/ |access-date=3 April 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=3 April 2022 |title=CeSid: Zabeležene nepravilnosti koje se tiču nepoštovanja procedura na izborima |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/cesid-zabelezene-nepravilnosti-koje-se-ticu-nepostovanja-procedura-na-izborima/ |access-date=3 April 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref> Later that evening, CRTA stated that multiple [[Bulgarian train]]s occurred during the vote, and that some ballot stations in Belgrade declined to cooperate with electoral observers.<ref>{{Cite web |date=3 April 2022 |title=Nedeljkov: Nepravilnosti zabeležene na 10 odsto biračkih mesta u Srbiji |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/nedeljkov-nepravilnosti-zabelezene-na-10-odsto-birackih-mesta-u-srbiji/ |access-date=3 April 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=3 April 2022 |title=CRTA: Uočen veliki broj nepravilnosti, bugarski voz, a u Beogradu odbili da sarađuju sa posmatračima |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/crta-uocen-veliki-broj-nepravilnosti-bugarski-voz-a-u-beogradi-odbili-da-saradjuju-sa-posmatracima/ |access-date=3 April 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref> OSE, a non-governmental organisation, stated that irregularities took place in Novi Sad.<ref>{{Cite web |date=3 April 2022 |title=Posmatrači OSE tvrde da su primetili niz nepravilnosti u Novom Sadu |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/posmatraci-ose-tvrde-da-su-primetili-niz-nepravilnosti-u-novom-sadu/ |access-date=3 April 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref> CRTA and political activists had also noted that the election day was marked by high tensions, verbal and in several places, such as Belgrade, physical violence.<ref>{{Cite web |date=3 April 2022 |title=Crta: Tenzije i nepravilnosti, izlaznost do 16 časova 42,1 odsto |url=https://www.vreme.com/vesti/crta-tenzije-i-nepravilnosti-izlaznost-do-16-casova-421-odsto/ |access-date=3 April 2022 |website=Vreme |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=3 April 2022 |title=Izborne nepravilnosti i na jugu - paralelni spiskovi u Nišu i Blacu |url=https://www.juznevesti.com/Politika/Izborne-nepravilnosti-i-na-jugu-paralelni-spiskovi-u-Nisu-i-Blacu.sr.html |access-date=3 April 2022 |website=Južne vesti |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=3 April 2022 |title=Izbori u Srbiji: Zabilježene nepravilnosti i napadi na stranačke zvaničnike |url=https://balkans.aljazeera.net/videos/2022/4/3/izbori-u-srbiji-zabiljezene-nepravilnosti-i-napadi-na-stranacke-zvanicnike |access-date=4 April 2022 |website=Al Jazeera |language=bs}}</ref> Dveri and SSP also reported irregularities in [[Niš]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Tasić |first=T. |date=3 April 2022 |title=Iz Dveri nepravilnosti na glasanju u Nišu prijavili policiji i posmatračima |url=https://www.juznevesti.com/Politika/Iz-Dveri-nepravilnosti-na-glasanju-u-Nisu-prijavili-policiji-i-posmatracima.sr.html |access-date=4 April 2022 |website=Južne vesti |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=3 April 2022 |title=Niška opozicija tvrdi da je mnogo nepravilnosti tokom glasanja, u GIK kažu da nijedna nije prijavljena |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/niska-opozicija-tvrdi-da-je-mnogo-nepravilnosti-tokom-glasanja-u-gik-kazu-da-nijedna-nije-prijavljena/ |access-date=4 April 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref> ENEMO had stated that [[intimidation]] and [[vote buying]] affected the results of the elections, and that the process of voter registration lacked transparency.<ref>{{Cite web |date=4 April 2022 |title=ENEMO: Zastrašivanja i kupovina glasova uticali na poverenje građana u izbore |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/enemo-zastrasivanja-i-kupovina-glasova-uticali-na-poverenje-gradjana-u-izbore/ |access-date=4 April 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref> Former SNS MP [[Bratislav Jugović]] and the leader of PSG, [[Pavle Grbović]], were physically attacked outside of voting stations.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Sokić |first=Ljubica |date=3 April 2022 |title=Napadnut poslanik SNS Bata Jugović u Čačku |url=https://nova.rs/vesti/hronika/napadnut-poslanik-sns-bata-jugovic-u-cacku/ |access-date=3 April 2022 |website=NOVA portal |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=3 April 2022 |title=Pretučen lider PSG, Grboviću razbijena glava ispred mesnog odbora SNS |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/napadnut-lider-psg-grbovicu-razbijena-glava-u-blizini-birackog-mesta/ |access-date=3 April 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref>

The PACE monitoring mission evaluated that the "fundamental freedoms were largely respected, and voters were presented diverse political options, but a number of shortcomings resulted in an uneven playing field, favouring the incumbents". PACE also noted that public sector employees were pressured to support the ruling party and that state resources were misused during the campaign period.<ref>{{Cite web |date=5 April 2022 |title=Council of Europe bodies observe national and local elections in Serbia |url=https://www.coe.int/en/web/portal/full-news/-/asset_publisher/y5xQt7QdunzT/content/council-of-europe-bodies-observe-national-and-local-elections-in-serbia |access-date=9 April 2022 |website=Council of Europe |language=en-GB |location=Strasbourg}}</ref> Kyriakos Hadjiyianni, the special coordinator and leader of the OSCE short-term observers, said that the campaign period was competitive though that the ruling party had undue advantage.<ref>{{Cite web |date=4 April 2022 |title=Serbia's elections offered diverse political options, but shortcomings led to an uneven playing field, international observers say |url=https://pace.coe.int/en/news/8663/serbia-s-elections-offered-diverse-political-options-but-shortcomings-led-to-an-uneven-playing-field-international-observers-say |access-date=10 April 2022 |website=Parliamentary Assembly of the Council of Europe}}</ref> According to [[Freedom House]], after the 2022 elections, Serbia ceased to be an [[electoral democracy]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Serbia: Freedom in the World 2023 Country Report |url=https://freedomhouse.org/country/serbia/freedom-world/2023 |access-date=25 December 2023 |website=Freedom House |language=en}}</ref>

Shortly after 23:00 (UTC+01:00), Vučić declared his victory.<ref>{{Cite web |date=3 April 2022 |title=Vučić: Srbija se dramatično pomerila u desno, razgovaraćemo i sa onima koji su najudaljeniji od nas |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/vucic-srbija-se-dramticno-pomerila-u-desno-razgovaracemo-i-sa-onima-koji-su-najudaljeniji-od-nas/ |access-date=3 April 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref> He announced in a televised victory speech, that he secured roughly 60% of the popular vote, adding, "I am pleased that a huge number of people voted and showed the democratic nature of Serbian society".<ref>{{Cite web |date=3 April 2022 |title=Serbia's incumbent President Vucic declares election victory |url=https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20220403-serbia-s-incumbent-president-vucic-declares-election-victory |access-date=3 April 2022 |website=France 24 |language=en}}</ref> After the proclamation of the preliminary results, Vučić was congratulated by [[Emmanuel Macron]], [[Vladimir Putin]], [[Miloš Zeman]], [[Zoran Milanović]], and others.<ref>{{Cite web |date=4 April 2022 |title=Svetski zvaničnici čestitali Vučiću pobedu na izborima |url=https://www.b92.net/info/izbori2022/vesti.php?yyyy=2022&mm=04&dd=04&nav_id=2134216 |access-date=4 April 2022 |website=B92 |language=sr-Latn-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=4 April 2022 |title=Putin čestitao Vučiću na izbornoj pobjedi |url=https://www.slobodnaevropa.org/a/putin-vucic-izbori-srbija/31785120.html |access-date=4 April 2022 |newspaper=Radio Slobodna Evropa |language=sr}}</ref> [[Milorad Dodik]] also congratulated him, after stating his support for him a few days prior to the election.<ref>{{Cite web |date=4 April 2022 |title=Dodik čestitao Vučiću: Svaki uspeh Srbije gledamo i kao uspeh Republike Srpske |url=https://www.b92.net/info/vesti/index.php?yyyy=2022&mm=04&dd=04&nav_category=167&nav_id=2134047 |access-date=4 April 2022 |website=B92 |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=31 March 2022 |title=Dodik podržao Vučića i SNS i poželeo mu pobedu na izborima u interesu kontinuiteta i stabilnosti |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/izbori22/dodik-podrzao-vucica-i-sns-i-pozeleo-mu-pobedu-na-izborima-u-interesu-kontinuiteta-i-stabilnosti/ |access-date=4 April 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref> The [[Ecological Uprising]] and Assembly of Free Serbia, who were a part of the We Must coalition, organised a protest in front of the RIK building on 4 April.<ref>{{Cite web |date=4 April 2022 |title=Održan protest ispred RIK-a, Ćuta traži javno prebrojavanje svih glasova |url=https://rs.n1info.com/izbori-2022/protest-ispred-rik-a-cuta-kaze-da-ce-traziti-javno-prebrojavanje-svih-glasova/ |access-date=6 April 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref> After the election, Ponoš left Narodna.<ref>{{Cite web |date=5 April 2022 |title=Zdravko Ponoš napustio Narodnu stranku |url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/zdravko-ponos-napustio-narodnu-stranku/ |access-date=6 April 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref> Further disagreements between the coalition partners in the UZPS coalition broke out, with [[Vuk Jeremić]] and his Narodna opposing the meeting between [[Dragan Đilas]] and Vučić.<ref>{{Cite web |date=20 April 2022 |title=Jeremić: Đilas se Vučiću stavio na raspolaganje |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/jeremic-djilas-se-vucicu-stavio-na-raspolaganje/ |access-date=23 April 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref> Tepić also accused Jeremić of populism.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Milenković |first=Mirjana |date=23 April 2022 |title=Marinika Tepić: Naši dojučerašnji partneri strmoglavili su se u populizam |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/marinika-tepic-nasi-dojucerasnji-partneri-strmoglavili-su-se-u-populizam/ |access-date=23 April 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref> This led to the dissolution of UZPS.<ref>{{Cite web |date=28 April 2022 |title=Grbović (PSG): Koalicija "Ujedinjeni za pobedu Srbije" praktično ne postoji |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/grbovic-psg-koalicija-ujedinjeni-za-pobedu-srbije-prakticno-ne-postoji/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220501213301/https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/grbovic-psg-koalicija-ujedinjeni-za-pobedu-srbije-prakticno-ne-postoji/ |archive-date=1 May 2022 |access-date=1 May 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref> In June 2022, Ćuta, Stojković, and Zelenović held a founding assembly of their political party, which was named [[Together (Serbia)|Together]].<ref name=":02">{{Cite web |date=11 June 2022 |title=Deo koalicije "Moramo" formirao političku organizaciju "Zajedno" |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/deo-koalicije-moramo-formirao-politicku-organizaciju-zajedno/ |access-date=11 June 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=11 June 2022 |title=Članice koalicije "Moramo" se ujedinile u "Zajedno" - stranku bez lidera |url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/clanice-koalicije-moramo-se-ujedinile-u-stranku-zajedno/ |access-date=11 June 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref>

=== Government formation ===
{{Main|Third cabinet of Ana Brnabić}}

Vučić was sworn in again as president on 31 May; during his speech he had stated that the government would be formed by the end of July and that the government would potentially impose [[International sanctions during the 2022 Russian invasion of Ukraine|sanctions on Russia]] due to the [[2022 Russian invasion of Ukraine]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=31 May 2022 |title=Vučić: Vlada do kraja jula, moraćemo da se bavimo sankcijama |url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/vucic-vlada-do-kraja-jula-moracemo-da-razmisljamo-o-sankcijama/ |access-date=31 May 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=31 May 2022 |title=Vučić najavio Vladu do kraja jula |url=https://www.slobodnaevropa.org/a/vucic-zakletva-srbija-predsednik/31875316.html |access-date=31 May 2022 |newspaper=Radio Slobodna Evropa |language=sr}}</ref> SPS confirmed that it would want to extend its cooperation with SNS, while the [[Democratic Alliance of Croats in Vojvodina]] (DSHV) and [[Alliance of Vojvodina Hungarians]] (VMSZ) also expressed their desire to join the government.<ref>{{Cite web |date=4 July 2022 |title=Dačić još nije razgovarao sa Vučićem o vladi: SPS spreman za nastavak saradnje |url=https://www.telegraf.rs/vesti/politika/3522271-dacic-jos-nije-razgovarao-sa-vucicem-o-vladi-sps-spreman-za-nastavak-saradnje |access-date=4 July 2022 |website=Telegraf |language=sr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=7 July 2022 |title=Žigmanov: SNS još uvek nije kontaktirala DSHV oko formiranja nove vlade |url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/zigmanov-sns-jos-uvek-nije-kontaktirala-dshv-oko-formiranja-nove-vlade/ |access-date=9 July 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=9 July 2022 |title=Ištvan Pastor: Spremni smo da budemo u novoj vlasti |url=https://nova.rs/vesti/politika/istvan-pastor-spremni-smo-da-budemo-u-novoj-vlasti/ |access-date=9 July 2022 |website=NOVA portal |language=sr-RS}}</ref> Vučić announced that consultations with all parliamentary lists would begin on 14 July.<ref>{{Cite web |date=8 July 2022 |title=Vučić 14. jula počinje konsultacije sa predstavnicima svih parlamentarnih lista |url=https://nova.rs/vesti/politika/vucic-14-jula-pocinje-konsultacije-sa-predstavnicima-svih-parlamentarnih-lista/ |access-date=9 July 2022 |website=NOVA portal |language=sr-RS}}</ref> The consultations lasted until 18 July.<ref>{{Cite web |date=18 July 2022 |title=Završetak konsultacija o kandidatu za budućeg premijera |url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/zavrsetak-konsultacija-o-kandidatu-za-buduceg-premijera/ |access-date=20 July 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref> The first constitutive session of the 2022–2026 convocation was held on 1 August.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Milenković |first=M. R. |date=27 July 2022 |title=Dačić sazvao konstitutivnu sednicu Skupštine Srbije za ponedeljak, prvi avgust |url=https://www.danas.rs/vesti/politika/sazvana-konstitutivna-sednica-parlamenta-za-1-avgust/ |access-date=28 July 2022 |website=Danas |language=sr-RS}}</ref> Brnabić received the mandate to form a new government on 27 August.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Kovačević |first=Emina |date=27 August 2022 |title=Ana Brnabić mandatar za sastav nove vlade |url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/ana-brnabic-mandatar-za-sastav-nove-vlade/ |access-date=27 August 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref> The composition of her [[Third cabinet of Ana Brnabić|cabinet]] was presented on 23 October, while the cabinet was sworn in on 26 October.<ref name="SNSm">{{cite news |last1=Sovrlić |first1=Sanja |date=23 October 2022 |title=Vučić saopštio predloge SNS za ministre |language=sr |work=N1 |url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/u-toku-sednica-go-sns-ocekuju-se-imena-ministara/ |access-date=23 October 2022}}</ref><ref name=":03">{{Cite web |date=25 October 2022 |title=Šta opozicija zamera predloženim ministrima, Brnabić odgovara Violom fon Kramon |url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/sta-opozicija-zamera-predlozenim-ministrima-brnabic-odgovara-violom-fon-kramon/ |access-date=25 October 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref><ref name=":15">{{Cite web |date=26 October 2022 |title=Poslanici izglasali novu Vladu Srbije |url=https://rs.n1info.com/vesti/poslanici-izglasali-novu-vladu-srbije/ |access-date=26 October 2022 |website=N1 |language=sr-RS}}</ref>

